course: dictionary
lesson: 11682
title: Atheism and belief
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name what people believe. Atheism is one of them. It comes from the Greek for "without god". «Many people in our class have different beliefs, and my friend has atheism as her belief.» This means she does not believe there is a God or any gods.
explain: Religious education lessons compare beliefs. «In RE we learned about atheism, theism and agnosticism.» Theism means believing in God. Agnosticism means not being sure whether God exists. Atheism is a clear "no" to God and gods.
explain: Atheists can still have strong values. «Atheists base their ideas of right and wrong on reason, kindness and human values.» Not believing in God does not mean having no morals. When you read about a belief, check the words around it to see what it means.
fact: Atheism means not believing in any god or gods.
fact: Atheism is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say "atheism", not "atheisms".
fact: Theism means believing in God; agnosticism means not being sure.
fact: Atheists often base their ideas of right and wrong on reason, kindness and human values.
exercise: «My cousin has atheism as her belief.» What does atheism mean here? | Being sure that God exists | Believing in many gods | *Not believing in any god | Going to a place of worship every week
exercise: «In RE we compare atheism with theism.» Find and copy the word that means believing in God. | atheism | compare | *theism | lesson
exercise: Tom says atheism means believing in lots of gods. Is he right? | Yes, it means believing in one god | Not sure, it is a kind of food | Yes, he is right | *No, atheism means not believing in any god
test: Atheists base their ideas of right and wrong on what? | *Reason, kindness and human values | Luck and chance | Only what the king says | Only the words of an old book
test: Which word means not being sure whether God exists? | *Agnosticism | Atheist | Theism | Atheism
exam: Which sentence uses atheism correctly? | Atheism is a lovely red flower in the garden | *Her belief in atheism means she does not believe in any god | We sang atheism in assembly today | He ran to atheism after the football match
